🧩 PART 1: CREATE USER ACCESS LIST

✅ Create new SharePoint list:

SE Access List


---

Columns:

Column Name	Type

Title	(optional)
Section	Lookup → SE Section List
User	Person or Group



---

🖥️ Example Data

Section     | User
-------------------------
PR INK      | King
PR INK      | Geryl
VP PR       | Chami
VP PR       | Hannah


---

🧩 PART 2: GET CURRENT USER

In Power Apps:

User().Email


---

🧩 PART 3: CHECK ACCESS

We will check:

👉 “Is current user allowed for selected section?”


---

✅ Create a variable

In Dropdown_Section.OnChange:

Set(
    varHasAccess,
    CountRows(
        Filter(
            'SE Access List',
            Section.Id = Dropdown_Section.Selected.ID &&
            User.Email = User().Email
        )
    ) > 0
)


---

🧩 PART 4: CONTROL ACCESS


---

✅ OPTION 1: DISABLE FORM

Select your main container (form area):

